# eslint-snapshot-rule-tester format: v1


Test: block-no-mismatched-edge >> invalid >>> docs/rules/block-no-mismatched-edge.md incorrect 1
Filename: block-no-mismatched-edge-incorrect-1.mmd

Code:
  1 | block
  2 |   A -- "x" ==> B
    |     ^~~~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  3 |

[1] mermaid.js takes this edge's line and markers only from the arrow after the label, losing part of the opening arrow.
    Suggestions:
      - Use the later arrow’s line in the opening arrow.
        Output:
          1 | block
          2 |   A == "x" ==> B
          3 |
      - Use the opening arrow’s line in the later arrow.
        Output:
          1 | block
          2 |   A -- "x" --> B
          3 |
---


